# Analysis plan: sample-pca

Status: APPROVED 2026-11-10

## Goal
See how the six samples cluster using PCA on gene counts, coloured by condition.

## Inputs
Resolve both input types again at execution time with `_system/resolve_artifact.py --project <project> --assay rnaseq_bulk --consumes counts_gene design`. Paths below are relative to the project and reflect the current resolution. Inputs remain read-only.

| Artifact type | Resolved from | Path |
|---|---|---|
| counts_gene | rnaseq_bulk / 01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper (native) | 02_bioinformatics/rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper/run/results/star_salmon/salmon.merged.gene_counts_length_scaled.tsv |
| design | 01_prepare_samplesheets (native) | 01_samplesheets/rnaseq_bulk_design.csv |

The design contains A1, A2, A3 (untreated) and B1, B2, B3 (treated).

## Method
1. After approval, implement `scripts/sample_pca.py` using Python with pandas, NumPy, scikit-learn and matplotlib in `gars-bio`, sourced through `_system/gars-env.sh`. Run every analysis step in the configured batch executor. Record input resolutions, parameters and package versions in the report. If dependencies are absent, stop without installing anything.
2. Load the resolved TSV count matrix and CSV design. Use `gene_id` as the gene identifier and exclude the `gene_name` annotation from numeric data. Require unique, nonempty gene and sample identifiers, exactly the six designed sample columns, complete condition labels, finite nonnegative counts and positive sample totals. Align count columns explicitly to design sample order; stop on any mismatch. Preserve fractional length-scaled counts without rounding.
3. Normalize each sample by its total gene count to counts per million (CPM = count / column sum * 1,000,000). Retain genes with CPM >= 1 in at least three of the six samples. Transform retained values as log2(CPM + 1); remove genes with zero variance across samples. Use every remaining gene, without selecting genes by condition or differential expression. Stop if fewer than two variable genes remain.
4. Transpose to samples by genes. Run `sklearn.decomposition.PCA(n_components=2, svd_solver="full", whiten=False)`, centering each gene across samples without scaling genes to unit variance. Conditions are used only for colouring and are not supplied to PCA.
5. Plot PC1 against PC2 with matplotlib (noninteractive Agg backend), one point per sample, coloured consistently by condition (untreated: #0072B2; treated: #D55E00), a condition legend and sample-ID labels. Include explained variance percentages on both axes. Save PNG at 300 dpi and vector PDF. No clustering algorithm or inferential test is included; this is an exploratory PCA projection.
6. Export sample scores (sample_id, condition, PC1, PC2) and explained variance (component, eigenvalue, explained_variance_ratio, explained_variance_percent). Write a short report documenting the method, six-sample mapping, genes before/after filtering, normalization totals, input provenance and figure links. Describe only the requested sample relationships in this projection, without causal or differential-expression claims. All generated files stay within this analysis directory.

